        "text": "All the requested Python files have been created successfully in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] upsert_document.py**: Upserts a JSON document by its primary identifier using AWS DynamoDB.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] fetch_document.py**: Fetches a document by identifier from a managed NoSQL store using AWS DynamoDB.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] query_documents.py**: Queries documents by a field value or partition-style key using AWS DynamoDB.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] conditional_update.py**: Applies a conditional or version-aware update to one stored document using AWS DynamoDB.\n5. **[HELPER] database_client.py**: Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for the Managed NoSQL Document Store.\n6. **[HELPER] database_models.py**: Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for the Managed NoSQL Document Store.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] record_summary.py**: Summarizes retrieved document records.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] record_text_safety.py**: Checks user-generated document fields for unsafe content.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] record_translate.py**: Translates user-facing document fields using AWS Translate.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] record_export_archive.py**: Archives exported document snapshots or attachments in managed object storage using AWS S3.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses AWS services to interact with the managed NoSQL document store, making the provider identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, and response parsing utilities. The later-step scored files handle additional operations on the retrieved documents.",
